RipsMath_CalculateEntryPayout
├── it result payout number is always between 1 and n inclusive.
├── it different entry numbers produce different payout numbers when a is odd and n is a power of two.
├── it should never revert for valid inputs.
├── when the payout number falls in the first tier
│   └── it should return the payout for that position.
├── when the payout number falls in a middle tier
│   └── it should return the payout for that position.
├── when the payout number falls in the last tier
│   └── it should return the payout for that position.
├── when the tier has a single payout
│   └── it should return the min payout.
└── when the tier has multiple payouts
    ├── when the rank is first in the tier
    │   └── it should return the min payout.
    ├── when the rank is last in the tier
    │   └── it should return the max payout.
    └── when the rank is in the middle of the tier
        └── it should linearly interpolate between min and max payout.
